pt and TypeScript applications for over 7 years now. I started my career at=
 a fintech startup where I built trading dashboards using vanilla JavaScrip=
t and jQuery, but quickly moved into React when it became mainstream around=
 2016.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Over the past 5 years, I've been=
 focused primarily on <strong>React ecosystem development</strong>. At my c=
urrent role as Senior Frontend Engineer at TechCorp, I've been leading the =
architecture of a multi-tenant SaaS platform serving over 2 million users. =
Our tech stack includes <strong>Next.js 14 with App Router, TypeScript, Rea=
ct Query for server state management, Zustand for client state, and a micro=
-frontend architecture</strong> using Module Federation.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">What's particularly exciting abo=
ut my recent work is that I've been <strong>instrumental in migrating our l=
egacy Redux codebase to a more modern state management approach</strong>. W=
e reduced our bundle size by 40% and improved our largest contentful paint =
by 1.2 seconds by strategically adopting React Query for server state and Z=
ustand for lighter client state management.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">I'm also passionate about <stron=
g>developer experience and tooling</strong> - I've built internal CLI tools=
 that automated our component generation, implemented advanced TypeScript p=
atterns for better type safety, and established testing strategies that imp=
roved our code coverage from 45% to 92%.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Th=
at's impressive! The migration from Redux to modern state management is som=
ething many teams struggle with. Before we dive deeper, could you tell me a=
bout a particularly challenging technical problem you've solved recently, a=
nd how you approached it?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Abso=
lutely! One of the most challenging problems I solved was <strong>optimizin=
g real-time data synchronization</strong> in our trading dashboard applicat=
ion. We had thousands of users simultaneously viewing live market data, and=
 our initial implementation was causing significant performance issues.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>The Problem</strong>: Ou=
r WebSocket connections were overwhelming the main thread, we had memory le=
aks from improper cleanup, and users were experiencing 3-5 second delays in=
 data updates. The Redux store was becoming a bottleneck with too many unne=
cessary re-renders.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>My Approach</strong>:</p=
>
