<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">Key Architecture=
 Decisions &amp; Trade-offs:</h3>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>1. Operational Transform=
 vs CRDT</strong>:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Chose OT</strong> becau=
se it provides deterministic conflict resolution and is well-understood</li=
>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Trade-off</strong>: Mor=
e complex than CRDTs but better performance for text editing</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>2. Zustand vs Redux for =
State Management</strong>:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Chose Zustand</strong> =
for lighter weight and better TypeScript integration</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Trade-off</strong>: Les=
s mature ecosystem than Redux but perfect for this use case</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>3. Real-time Synchroniza=
tion Strategy</strong>:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Hybrid approach</strong=
>: Local-first with server reconciliation</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Trade-off</strong>: Mor=
e complex but provides better user experience</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>4. Cursor Position Calcu=
lation</strong>:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>DOM-based measurement</=
strong> for accuracy</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Trade-off</strong>: Per=
formance cost but necessary for precise positioning</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Performance Characterist=
ics</strong>:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>O(n)</strong> operation=
 transformation complexity</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Minimal re-renders</str=
ong> through strategic memoization</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Efficient WebSocket usa=
ge</strong> with operation batching</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Memory management</stro=
ng> through operation history limits</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This implementation provides a <=
strong>production-ready foundation</strong> for collaborative editing with =
proper conflict resolution, undo/redo functionality, and real-time user pre=
sence indicators.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ou=
tstanding implementation! Your operational transform logic is particularly =
impressive, and I love how you've structured the separation between local o=
perations and server synchronization.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me ask a few follow-up quest=
ions to go deeper:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>How would you handle ne=
twork partitions?</strong> What if a user goes offline for 10 minutes, make=
s extensive changes, then comes back online while others have also been edi=
ting?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>What about performance =
at scale?</strong> If you had 100 users editing simultaneously, what bottle=
necks would you expect and how would you optimize?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>How would you extend th=
is to support rich text formatting</strong> (bold, italic, links) while mai=
ntaining the operational transform correctness?</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Exce=
llent follow-up questions! These are exactly the challenges you'd face when=
 scaling a collaborative editor to production. Let me address each systemat=
ically:</p>
